# Translation System Rules

## Overview

BitTasker uses svelte-i18n for internationalization with automatic translation capabilities. **ALWAYS translate new text content** and follow these patterns for consistent multilingual support.

## Core Principles

### 1. **ALWAYS Translate New Text**

- **NEVER hardcode text strings** in components
- **ALWAYS use translation keys** for all user-facing text
- **ALWAYS add translations** for new features
- **ALWAYS test** in both English and Spanish
- **ALWAYS** ensure translated text is reactive

### 2. **Translation Key Patterns**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Use descriptive, hierarchical keys
$t('dashboard.tasks.create.title')
$t('auth.login.form.email_label')
$t('common.buttons.save')

// ❌ WRONG - Don't use generic or unclear keys
$t('title')
$t('button')
$t('text')
```

### 3. **Namespace Organization**

```text
locales/
├── en/
│   ├── common.json          # Shared UI elements
│   ├── auth.json           # Authentication
│   ├── dashboard/          # Dashboard features
│   │   ├── dashboard.json
│   │   ├── tasks/
│   │   ├── bids/
│   │   └── wallet/
│   ├── company/            # Company pages
│   └── taskees/            # Taskee-specific content
└── es/                     # Spanish translations
    └── [same structure]
```

## Implementation Patterns

### 1. **Basic Translation Usage**

```svelte
<script>
  import { t } from 'svelte-i18n';
</script>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<h1>{$t('dashboard.tasks.create.title')}</h1>
<button class="btn btn-primary">{$t('common.buttons.create')}</button>

<!-- ❌ WRONG -->
<h1>Create Task</h1>
<button class="btn btn-primary">Create</button>
```

### 2. **Translation with Variables**

```svelte
<script>
  import { t } from 'svelte-i18n';
  
  let taskCount = $state(5);
  let userName = $state('John');
</script>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<p>{$t('dashboard.tasks.count', { count: taskCount })}</p>
<p>{$t('dashboard.welcome.message', { name: userName })}</p>
```

### 3. **Conditional Translations**

```svelte
<script>
  import { t } from 'svelte-i18n';
  
  let isCompleted = $state(false);
</script>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<span class="badge" class:badge-success={isCompleted} class:badge-warning={!isCompleted}>
  {$t(isCompleted ? 'common.status.completed' : 'common.status.pending')}
</span>
```

### 4. **Form Validation Messages**

```svelte
<script>
  import { t } from 'svelte-i18n';
  
  let email = $state('');
  let emailError = $state('');
</script>

<input 
  type="email" 
  bind:value={email}
  class="input" 
  class:input-error={emailError}
  placeholder={$t('auth.login.form.email_placeholder')}
/>
{#if emailError}
  <div class="text-error text-sm">{$t('auth.login.form.email_error')}</div>
{/if}
```

